hadiths[109]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2170","It was narrated from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade Mulamasah and Munabadhah. (Sahih) Sahl added: ""Sufyan said: 'Mulamasah means when a man touches something with his hand without seeing it"
"2171","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Let one of you not undersell another"
"2172","lt was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""A man is not to undersell his brother"
"2173","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that :the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade the Najsh"
"2174","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet said:""Do not practice Najsh"
"2175","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""A City-dweller should not sell for a Bedouin"
"2176","It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""A city-dweller should not sell for a Bedouin. Leave people to (engage in trade) and Allah will grant them provision through one another"
"2177","Ibn Tawus narrated from his father that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade a city-dweller to sell for a Bedouin."" (Sahih)I (Tawus) said to Ibn 'Abbas: ""What is meant by the words: 'A city-dweller selling for a Bedouin?' He said: ""He should not be a broker for him"
"2178","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""Do not meet the traders on the way"
"2179","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade meeting traders on the way"
"2180","It was narrated that 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade. meeting the owners of goods (away from the market)"
"2181","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah said:""When two men enter into a transaction"
"2182","It was narrated from Abu Barzah Al-Aslami that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:”The two parties to a transaction have the choice (of annulling it) so long as they have not yet parted"
"2183","It was narrated from Samurah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""The two parties to a transaction have the choice (of annulling it) so long as they have not yet parted"
"2184","It was narrated that Jabir bin' Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) bought a load of fodder from a Bedouin man. When the transaction was concluded"
"2185","It was narrated from Dawud bin Salih Al Madani that his father said:I heard Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri say: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Transactions may only be done by mutual consent"
"2186","It was narrated from Qasim bin 'Abdur Rahman from his father that :Abdullah bin Mas'ud sold one of the slaves from the state[1] to Ash'ath bin Qais"
"2187","It was narrated that Hakim bin Hizam said:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"2188","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"2189","It was narrated from 'Ata that 'Attab bin Asid said that :when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent him to Makkah"
"2190","It was narrated from 'Uqbah bin 'Amir or Samurah bin Jundab that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Any man who sells to two men"
"2191","It was narrated from Samurah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2192","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"2193","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu'aib"
"2194","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade Gharar transaction sand Hasah transactions"
"2195","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade Gharar transactions"
"2196","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade selling what is in the wombs of cattle until they give birth"
"2197","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that :the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade selling Hablul-Habalah"
"2198","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that :a man from among the Ansar came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and begged from him. He said"
"2199","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:Whoever agrees with a Muslim to cancel a transaction Allah will forgive his sins on the Day of Resurrection"
"2200","It was nanated that Anas bin Malik said:""Prices rose during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2201","It was narrated that Abu Sa'eed said:""Prices rose at the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2202","Uthman bin 'Affan narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Allah will admit to Paradise a man who was lenient when he sold and when he bought"
"2203","It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""May Allah have mercy on a person who is lenient when he sells"
"2204","It was narrated that Qailah Umm Bani Anmar said:""I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2205","It was narrated that Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:""I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) on a military campaign"
"2206","It was narrated that 'Ali said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade haggling before sunrise"
"2207","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""There are three to whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection"
"2208","It was narrated from Abu Dharr that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""There are three to whom Allah will not speak on the Day of Resurrection nor will He look at them or purify them"
"2209","It was narrated from Abu Qatadah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2210","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Whoever buys a palm tree that has been pollinated"
"2211","It was narrated from Salim bin 'Abdullah"
"2212","It was narrated from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""Whoever sells a palm tree and sells a slave."" Mentioning both of them together"
"2213","It was narrated that 'Ubadah bin Samit said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled that the fruit of a palm tree belongs to the one who pollinated it"
"2214","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Do not sell fruits until they have ripened."" And he forbade (both) the seller and the purchaser (to engage in such a transaction)"
"2215","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Do not sell fruits until they have ripened"
"2216","It was narrated from Jabir that :the Prophet (ﷺ) forbade selling fruits until they have ripened"
"2217","It was narrated from Anas bin Malik that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade selling fruits until they have changed the color"
"2218","It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade selling for many years ahead"
"2219","It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""Whoever sells fruits then the crop fails"
"2220","It was narrated that Suwaid bin Qais said:""Makhrafah Al' Abdi and I brought linens from Hajar[1] The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to us to bargain with us with some trousers. There was someone with me who weighed (the goods) in exchange for a wage. So the Prophet (ﷺ) said to the one weighing: 'Weigh and add more"
"2221","It was narrated that Simak bin Harb said:""I heard Malik Abu Safwan bin 'Umairah"
"2222","It was narrated from Jabir bin 'Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:""When you weigh"
"2223","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:""When the Prophet (ﷺ) came to Al-Madinah"
"2224","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by a man who was selling food. He put his hand in it and saw that there was something wrong with it. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said"
"2225","It was narrated that Abu Hamra' said:""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pass by a man having food in a vessel. He put his hand in it and said: 'Perhaps you are cheating. Whoever cheats us is not one of us"
"2226","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:""Whoever buys food"
"2436","It was narrated from 'Aisha that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) bought some food from a Jew with payment to be made later"
"2437","It was narrated that Anas said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pawned his armor to a jew in Al-Madinah"
"2438","It was narrated from Asma' bin Yazid that:the Prophet (ﷺ) died while his armor was pawned to a Jew for food"
"2439","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that:the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) died while his armor was pawned to a Jew for thirty Sa’s of barley.' ”"
"2440","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“A mount may be ridden when it is pawned"
"2441","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Do not forfeit items held in pledge.”"
"2442","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:(Allah (SWT) says:) “I am the opponent of three on the Day of Resurrection"
"2443","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Give the worker his wages before his sweat dries.”"
"2444","It was narrated that 'Ali bin Rabah said:“I heard 'Utbah bin Nuddar say: 'We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he recited Ta-Sin. When he reached the story of Musa"
"2445","Salim bin Hayyan said:I heard Abu Hurairah say: “I grew up an orphan"
"2446","It was narrated that Ibn 'Abbas said:“The Prophet (ﷺ) was in need of food"
"2447","It was narrated that 'Ali said:“I used to draw water"
"2448","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:“A man from among the Ansar Came and said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2449","It was narrated that Rafi 'bin Khadji said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade Muhaqalah and Muzabanah"
"2450","It was narrated that 'Amr bin Dinar said:“I heard Ibn 'Umar say: 'We used to lend land for cultivation in return for a share of the harvest"
"2451","Ata' said:“I heard Jabir bin 'Abdullah say: Some men among us had extra land which they would rent out for one third or one quarter (of the crop). The Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Whoever has extra land"
"2452","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever has land"
"2453","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that:he used to lease out some land that belonged to him"
"2454","It was narrated that Jabir bin 'Abdullah said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) addressed us and said: 'Whoever has land"
"2455","It was narrated from Abu Sufyan"
"2456","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that he heard that people were leasing out land more. He said:“Subhan-Allah"
"2457","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“If one of you were to lend his brother his land"
"2458","It was narrated that Hazalah bin Qais said:“I asked Rafi' bin Khadij and he said: 'We used to lease out land on the basis that you would have what is produced by this piece of land"
"2459","Rafi'bin Khadi'j narrated that his paternal uncle Zuhair said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade us from doing something that was convenient for us.” I said: “What the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said is true.” He said that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “What do you with your farms?” We said: “We rent them out for one third or one quarter of their yield"
"2460","It was narrated from Usaid bin Zuhair"
"2461","Zaid bin Thabit said:“May Allah (SWT) forgive Rafi' bin Khadij. By Allah (SWT)! I have more knowledge of Ahadith than he does. Two men who had quarreled came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: 'If this is your situation"
"2462","It was narrated that 'Amr bin Dinar said:I said to Tawus: “O Abu 'Abdur-Rahman"
"2463","It was narrated from Tawus that :Mu`adh bin Jabl leased some land during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2465","It was narrated that Rafi` bin khadij said:We used to give land in return for food at the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2466","It was narrated that Rafi` bin Khadij said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever cultivates people`s land without their permission"
"2467","It was narrated from Ibn `Umar that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered into a contract with the people of Khaibar for one half of the fruits or crops yielded"
"2468","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:“When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave Khaibar to its people in return of its palm trees and land"
"2469","It was narrated that Anas bin Malik said:“When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) conquered Khaibar"
"2470","It was narrated from Simak that the heard Musa bin Talhah bin `Ubaidullah narrating that his father said:“I passed by some palm trees with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he saw some people pollinating the trees. He said: 'What are these people doing?' They said: 'They are taking something from the male part (of the plant) and putting it in the female part.' He said: 'I do not think that this will do any good.' News of that reached them"
"2471","It was narrated from 'Aisha that the Prophet (ﷺ) heard some sounds and said:“What is this noise?” They said: “Palm trees that are being pollinated.” He said: “If they did not do that it would be better.” So they did not pollinate them that year"
"2472","It was narrated from Ibn 'Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The Muslims are partners in three things: water"
"2473","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Three things cannot be denied to anyone: water"
"2474","It was narrated that 'Aishah said:“O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"2475","It was narrated from Abyad bin Hammal:That he asked for a salt flat called the Ma'rib Dam to be given to him"
"2478","It was narrated from Abu Hurairah that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“No one of you should withhold surplus water from common pastureland.”"
"2479","It was narrated from Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Surplus water should not be withheld"
"2480","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Zubair that :a man from among the Ansar had a dispute with Zubair in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) concerning the streams of the Harrah with which he irrigated his palm trees. The Ansari said: “Let the water flow"
"2481","It was narrated that Tha'labah bin Abu Malik said:“The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled concerning the stream of Mahzur that the higher ground took precedence over the lower"
"2482","It was narrated from 'Amr bin Shu`aib"
"2483","It was narrated from 'Ubadah bin Samit that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled concerning the irrigation of palm trees from streams"
"2484","It was narrated from Kathir bin 'Abdullah bin 'Amr bin 'Awf Al-Muzani"
"2485","It was narrated from Ibn `Abbas that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Every division that was allocated according to (the rules of) the Ignorance days"
"2486","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin Mughaffal that the Prophet (ﷺ) said:“Whoever digs a well"
"2487","It was narrated from Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“The land around a well (that is considered to be part of it) is the length of the well rope (in all directions).”"
"2488","It was narrated from 'Ubadah bin Samit that :the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled concerning one"
"2489","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah Said:“The land around a date-palm tree"
"2491","It was narrated from Hudhaifah bin Yaman that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:“Whoever sells a house and does not use the money for something similar"